mission "A Sea Worth Keeping"
    name "A Sea Worth Keeping"
    description "Return to Port Royal with the council's compact and choose how the secret of the drowned kingdom will be shared."
    source "San Telmo"
    destination "Port Royal"
    reward 2240
    speaker offer "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker visit "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    speaker complete "Commodore Anne Bonny"
    to offer
        has "The Crown's True Owner: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The council's compact is ready to be carried home. The secret of the drowned kingdom is no longer held by one archive or one captain, but the islands must still agree how much to share.`
            `Commodore Bonny reads the compact once more. "We can publish the whole chart, seal it away, or share only what navigators need to avoid danger. None of those choices is without a cost. I would rather the islands decide together than have a governor decide for them."`
            choice
                `"Very well. I will take responsibility for the next leg."`
                    accept
                `"Tell me the part you have not put on the table."`
                    goto details
                `"I will not be drawn into it. Good day."`
                    close
            label details
                `She folds the compact and gives it to you. "Take this to Port Royal and put it before the captains and councils. The secret must be handled carefully; it should not become another excuse for conquest."`
                choice
                    `"Then let us stop talking and set sail."`
                        accept
                    `"Not for me. Let another captain take the work."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Sea Worth Keeping. Return to Port Royal with the council's compact and choose how the secret of the drowned kingdom will be shared."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Port Royal, the councils and free captains review the compact and agree how the secret will be shared. Bonny watches the last signatures dry. "We have chosen to keep the knowledge in common, and to put the safety of the islands before any claim to glory."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Bonny looks out toward the harbour. "The chart will travel, but no one will own the sea. There will still be storms, privateers, and foolish governors. At least now there is a charter to remind them that these waters are lived in, not merely crossed."`
        log "Completed A Sea Worth Keeping. Received 2240 gold. Return to Port Royal with the council's compact and choose how the secret of the drowned kingdom will be shared."
